Q: How to convert a CodeIgniter query result object into an array of objects and pass it into the view file A: <p>Controller:</p>

<pre><code>function my_feeds()
    {   
        $this-&gt;load-&gt;model('membership_model');
        $query = $this-&gt;membership_model-&gt;get_my_feeds();
        if($query-&gt;num_rows()&gt;0) {
            $this-&gt;data['feed'] = $query;
            $this-&gt;load-&gt;view('my_feed');
        }
</code></pre>

<p>View:</p>

<pre><code>&lt;?php foreach($feed as $value) : ?&gt;
   &lt;td&gt; &lt;?=$value-&gt;nameofcolumn;?&gt; &lt;/td&gt;
&lt;?php endforeach; ?&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: Setting the WPF ComboBoxItem Background Color when an ObjectDataProvider binding is used to populate ComboBox A: <p>I investigated things even though this is not a task and the only thing left is to remove that default color and make transparent color of the selected item and when the mouse is over and it can be done like this(adding a style without custom control implementation but you will decide what you need).</p>
<p><a href="https://i.sstatic.net/CbzO9Hnr.png" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/CbzO9Hnr.png" alt="enter image description here" /></a></p>
<pre><code>&lt;Window
    x:Class=&quot;WPFExamples.MainWindow&quot;
    xmlns=&quot;http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation&quot;
    xmlns:x=&quot;http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml&quot;
    xmlns:d=&quot;http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008&quot;
    xmlns:local=&quot;clr-namespace:WPFExamples&quot;
    xmlns:mc=&quot;http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006&quot;
    xmlns:sys=&quot;clr-namespace:System;assembly=mscorlib&quot;
    Title=&quot;MainWindow&quot;
    Width=&quot;800&quot;
    Height=&quot;450&quot;
    mc:Ignorable=&quot;d&quot;&gt;

    &lt;Window.Resources&gt;

        &lt;!--  Enum source  --&gt;
        &lt;ObjectDataProvider
            x:Key=&quot;ColorEnumValues&quot;
            MethodName=&quot;GetValues&quot;
            ObjectType=&quot;{x:Type sys:Enum}&quot;&gt;
            &lt;ObjectDataProvider.MethodParameters&gt;
                &lt;x:Type TypeName=&quot;local:MyColorEnum&quot; /&gt;
            &lt;/ObjectDataProvider.MethodParameters&gt;
        &lt;/ObjectDataProvider&gt;

        &lt;!--  Enum → Brush converter  --&gt;
        &lt;local:EnumValueColorConverter x:Key=&quot;ItemColorConverter&quot; /&gt;

        &lt;!--  Custom ComboBoxItem Style  --&gt;
        &lt;Style x:Key=&quot;ColoredComboBoxItemStyle&quot; TargetType=&quot;ComboBoxItem&quot;&gt;

            &lt;!--  Remove default focus visuals  --&gt;
            &lt;Setter Property=&quot;FocusVisualStyle&quot; Value=&quot;{x:Null}&quot; /&gt;

            &lt;!--  Background from enum  --&gt;
            &lt;Setter Property=&quot;Background&quot; Value=&quot;{Binding Converter={StaticResource ItemColorConverter}}&quot; /&gt;

            &lt;Setter Property=&quot;BorderBrush&quot; Value=&quot;Transparent&quot; /&gt;
            &lt;Setter Property=&quot;BorderThickness&quot; Value=&quot;0&quot; /&gt;
            &lt;Setter Property=&quot;Foreground&quot; Value=&quot;White&quot; /&gt;

            &lt;Setter Property=&quot;Template&quot;&gt;
                &lt;Setter.Value&gt;
                    &lt;ControlTemplate TargetType=&quot;ComboBoxItem&quot;&gt;
                        &lt;Border
                            x:Name=&quot;Border&quot;
                            Padding=&quot;4&quot;
                            Background=&quot;{TemplateBinding Background}&quot;
                            BorderBrush=&quot;{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}&quot;
                            BorderThickness=&quot;{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}&quot;&gt;

                            &lt;ContentPresenter HorizontalAlignment=&quot;Left&quot; VerticalAlignment=&quot;Center&quot; /&gt;
                        &lt;/Border&gt;

                        &lt;ControlTemplate.Triggers&gt;

                            &lt;!--  Selected: show border only  --&gt;
                            &lt;Trigger Property=&quot;IsSelected&quot; Value=&quot;True&quot;&gt;
                                &lt;Setter TargetName=&quot;Border&quot; Property=&quot;BorderBrush&quot; Value=&quot;Black&quot; /&gt;
                                &lt;Setter TargetName=&quot;Border&quot; Property=&quot;BorderThickness&quot; Value=&quot;2&quot; /&gt;
                            &lt;/Trigger&gt;

                            &lt;!--  Mouse over: subtle border  --&gt;
                            &lt;Trigger Property=&quot;IsMouseOver&quot; Value=&quot;True&quot;&gt;
                                &lt;Setter TargetName=&quot;Border&quot; Property=&quot;BorderBrush&quot; Value=&quot;Gray&quot; /&gt;
                                &lt;Setter TargetName=&quot;Border&quot; Property=&quot;BorderThickness&quot; Value=&quot;1&quot; /&gt;
                            &lt;/Trigger&gt;

                        &lt;/ControlTemplate.Triggers&gt;
                    &lt;/ControlTemplate&gt;
                &lt;/Setter.Value&gt;
            &lt;/Setter&gt;

        &lt;/Style&gt;

    &lt;/Window.Resources&gt;

    &lt;Grid Margin=&quot;10&quot;&gt;

        &lt;ComboBox
            Width=&quot;200&quot;
            Height=&quot;30&quot;
            ItemContainerStyle=&quot;{StaticResource ColoredComboBoxItemStyle}&quot;
            ItemsSource=&quot;{Binding Source={StaticResource ColorEnumValues}}&quot;
            SelectedIndex=&quot;0&quot; /&gt;

    &lt;/Grid&gt;
&lt;/Window&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: Despite passing $data from my controller to my view in CodeIgniter, $data is an undefined variable in my view file A: <p>Write this in your model function:</p>

<pre><code>$query = $this-&gt;db-&gt;get('cliente');
$data = $query-&gt;result_array();
return $data;
</code></pre>

<p>And this in your controller:</p>

<pre><code>$data['client']= $this-&gt;cliente_model-&gt;obtenerDatos();
$this-&gt;load-&gt;view('cliente_view',$data);
</code></pre>

<p>Then add this to your view:</p>

<pre><code>&lt;?php if ($client): foreach($client as $fila):?&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;?php echo $fila['correoCliente1'];?&gt;&lt;/td&gt; 
</code></pre>

<p>etc...</p>

<p>As you will see, <code>$data['client']</code> is now holding your database info, and you can read it by looping through the associative array in your view. More info on query builder class <a href="https://www.codeigniter.com/userguide3/database/query_builder.html#query-builder-class" rel="nofollow noreferrer">here</a>.</p>

Q: No breakpoints when using Xdebug in VSCode to a Apache server running in VirtualBox A: <p>I found hostname in config</p>
<p><a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/77842644/set-up-remote-debugging-with-php-7-2-and-xdebug-2-0">Set up remote debugging with PHP 7.2 and Xdebug 2.0</a></p>
<pre><code>{
    &quot;version&quot;: &quot;0.2.0&quot;,
    &quot;configurations&quot;: [
        {
            &quot;name&quot;: &quot;Listen for Xdebug&quot;,
            &quot;type&quot;: &quot;php&quot;,
            &quot;request&quot;: &quot;launch&quot;,
            &quot;hostname&quot;: &quot;10.0.2.2&quot;, //Remote server IP
            &quot;port&quot;: 9000
        }
    ]
}
</code></pre>

Q: WPF ListView items not displaying data from Binding (showing blank or wrong values)&quot; A: <p>Be sure that your DataContext instance of the <code>ListView</code> is set properly because perhaps you are using something directly from the View Model or perhaps your DataContext should be set to some kind of ancestor. Be sure too that your <code>ItemSource</code> of the control is being set as a <code>ObservableCollection&lt;YourModelClass&gt;</code> and to fix that binding to this <code>ItemSource={Binding MyPeople}</code> . You can find an example with explicit DataContext set if your binding objects are being defined in the View Model.</p>
<pre><code>&lt;ListView Margin=&quot;10&quot;
          ItemsSource=&quot;{Binding MyPeople, UpdateSourceTrigger=PropertyChanged}&quot;
          SelectedItem=&quot;{Binding ChosenPerson, UpdateSourceTrigger=PropertyChanged}&quot;&gt;
    &lt;ListView.DataContext&gt;
        &lt;vm:MainViewModel/&gt;
    &lt;/ListView.DataContext&gt;
    &lt;ListView.ItemTemplate&gt;
        &lt;DataTemplate&gt;
            &lt;Grid&gt;
                &lt;Grid.ColumnDefinitions&gt;
                    &lt;ColumnDefinition Width=&quot;*&quot; /&gt;
                    &lt;ColumnDefinition Width=&quot;*&quot; /&gt;
                &lt;/Grid.ColumnDefinitions&gt;

                &lt;TextBlock Text=&quot;{Binding Name}&quot; /&gt;
                &lt;TextBlock Grid.Column=&quot;1&quot;
                           Text=&quot;{Binding LastName}&quot; /&gt;
            &lt;/Grid&gt;
        &lt;/DataTemplate&gt;
    &lt;/ListView.ItemTemplate&gt;
&lt;/ListView&gt;
</code></pre>
